{"id":"d5b9dd3c-60cb-4ca4-a416-f821ea105e81","article_key":"doi:10.1038/s41562-026-02551-z","title":"Genome-wide analysis of social behaviour across social domains, reporters and developmental stages: a meta-regression approach","title_zh":"跨社会领域、报告者和发展阶段的社会行为全基因组分析：一种元回归方法","doi":"10.1038/s41562-026-02551-z","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-026-02551-z","abstract":"Abstract Social behaviour is a heritable trait linked to well-being and mental health, yet it varies across social context, including social domains, informants and development, which may shape its underlying genomic architecture. Here, we conducted a genome-wide meta-regression meta-analysis of social behaviour from infancy to early adulthood, studying ~500,000 repeated measures in European-ancestry cohorts ( N = 73,321). We modelled heterogeneity in single-variant associations across social domains (low prosocial behaviour and peer/social difficulties), multiple informants (parents, teachers and self-reports) and ages (2–29 years), identifying 6 associated loci, including variation within CADM2 ( P = 2.51 × 10 −9 ). Single nucleotide polymorphism-based heritability ranged from 2% to 7%, and the genetic architecture comprised 4 factors reflecting differences in either social domains or informants. Polygenic scores ( N = 16,305) accurately predicted contextual variation in independent cohorts, with some cross-ancestry transferability. Context-specific patterns of genetic correlations, particularly when estimating the developmental onset of associations, offer opportunities to disentangle shared trajectories linking social behaviour with later-life and mental health outcomes.","abstract_zh":"摘要 社会行为是一种可遗传的特质，与福祉和心理健康相关，但它在社会情境中存在差异，包括社会领域、信息来源和发展阶段，这可能塑造其潜在的基因组结构。在本研究中，我们对从婴儿期到早期成年期的社会行为进行了全基因组元回归元分析，研究了约50万条重复测量数据，来自欧洲血统人群（N = 73,321）。我们对单一变异与社会领域（低亲社会行为和同伴/社会困难）、多种信息来源（父母、教师和自我报告）以及年龄（2–29岁）之间的异质性进行了建模，识别出6个相关位点，其中包括CADM2内的变异（P = 2.51 × 10⁻⁹）。基于单核苷酸多态性（SNP）的遗传率从2%到7%不等，遗传架构由4个因子组成，反映了社会领域或信息来源的差异。多基因得分（N = 16,305）能够准确预测独立队列中的情境变异，并具有一定的跨种族可转移性。特定情境的遗传相关性模式，尤其是在估计关联的发育起始时，提供了机会来解开将社会行为与后期生活和心理健康结果联系的共享轨迹。","snippet":"Abstract Social behaviour is a heritable trait linked to well-being and mental health, yet it varies across social context, including social domains, informants and development, which may shape its underlying genomic architecture. Here, we conducted a genome-wide meta-regression meta-analysis of social behaviour from infancy to early adulthood, studying ~500,000 repeated measures in European-ancestry cohorts ( N = 7…","translated_at":"2026-09-22T22:38:28.286486Z","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":null,"issue":null,"published_at":"2026-09-21T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-09-22T20:14:31Z","display_date":"2026-09-22T20:14:31Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":"2026-09-21T00:00:00","print_published_at":null,"first_author":"Lucía de Hoyos","authors_text":"Lucía de Hoyos, Fenja Schlag, Sanjeevan Jahagirdar, Elizabeth C. Corfield, Andrea G. Allegrini, Danielle Admiraal, Eveline L. de Zeeuw, Ilja M. Nolte, Natalia Llonga, Alexander Neumann, Katherine Lange, Simone van den Bedem, Ebba Du Rietz, Ehsan Motazedi, Else Eising, Nicole Y. T. Ng, Teemu Palviainen, Carol A. Wang, Elisabeth Thiering, Sofia Scatolin, Priyanka Choudhary, Natalia Vilor-Tejedor, Zhijie Liao, Silvia Alemany, Casper-Emil T. Pedersen, Nora Fernandez-Jimenez, Megan L. Campbell, Polina Girchenko, Eli Barthome, L. Caitlin Martin, Hanna Seelemeyer, Afsheen Kumar, Alexandre Jeanne, Tarunveer S. Ahluwalia, Melissa H. Black, Jan K. Buitelaar, Simon E. Fisher, Anni Heiskala, María Hernández-Lorca, Vincent W. Jaddoe, Marjo-Riitta Järvelin, Sheri-Michelle Koopowitz, Marilyn T. Lake, Paul Lichtenstein, Sabrina Llop, Mannan Luo, Anni Malmberg, Sergi Marí, Albertine J. Oldehinkel, Zdenka Pausova, Craig E. Pennell, Robert Plomin, Ted Reichborn-Kjennerud, Sheena Reilly, Alina Rodriguez, Thomas Rolland, Angelic